  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI upgraded from 1.1.25 to 1.26.0 (Ubuntu packages from matrix.org, no workes) . Since then I can't verfiy the login for my user anymore. After entering the passphrase in element browser client (1.7.20 firefox/chrome) or desktop client (1.7.20) \"**Verify this login\" is loading for ever** (tested on different plattforms). If I skip verification at login and do a \"Connect this session to key backup\" afterwards I can load the keys from the backup with my passphrase and can decrypt encrypted messages. So the passphrase must be right. The strange thing is, that this happens only with my userid, other userids seem not to be affected. I don't see any errors in synapse log, nor in nginx log. Any ideas?\r\n",
